**Definition 3.2 (selection at partial cuts).** Use CYCLE Definitions
6.1–6.2's exact cell/slot/relation schemas, ordering and deduplication.
Construction roles are identified by the acquired static directory,
folded over an already derived literal native history. On an EX, record
the old R as constructed backing immediately, even before WR. The fresh
trailing R is boundary context, not an input bit. Close a span only at
its actual seal/completion; incomplete descriptors retain raw tracks
and absent parsed fields. The initial69 family stops at its constructed
initial endpoint, not at later staging. Stage publications use the same
sender/receiver roles in family5. A referenced remote endpoint carries
identity only, not its payload or a read permission.

The family4 pending record contains exactly the designated input site
and bit after its IN and before its matching WR. Outside that interval
it is empty. Length tests use their distinct latch. A pending mode bit
is not inferred from a later parsed frame, and an allocated source
payload zero is not inferred to be a consumed input. This is the same
footprint restriction as the actual reader, not a new historical latch
archive. PC, raw ingress scratch and marked positions remain present
as selected existing frontier data, although §4 will not need to assume
that an endpoint descriptor or endpoint frontier has finished.

